    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Brice Turang** stands as our premier play at 2B. With a robust efficiency score of 68.60, **Brice Turang** benefits significantly from facing Ray, whose 4.98 xERA suggests a volatile outing that favors our aggressive approach to stolen base accumulation. Despite the inherent risk of a L/L matchup, **Brice Turang**\u2019s placement in the #2 hole provides the necessary plate appearances to capitalize on Ray's pitch count, cementing his status as a \"Strong\" start. While other core pieces like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** are subject to the schedule volatility of this late-season date, the optimizer remains locked on maximizing daily efficiency to maintain our rotisserie edge.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was keeping **Travis Bazzana** on the bench. With a score of 31.86, **Travis Bazzana** fell well below our established 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" for active roster spots. The primary drag on his projection was the matchup against Smith, whose 3.07 xERA indicates a high-tier arm that drastically suppresses offensive upside. When factoring in the L/L platoon disadvantage and **Travis Bazzana** hitting toward the bottom of the order, it was mathematically prudent to bench him rather than risk burning game caps on a low-efficiency start. Meanwhile, **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined due to his absence from today\u2019s confirmed lineup, reinforcing our strict discipline in starting only those players positioned to provide immediate value in the 5x5 categories.",
